# 
# https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#FinancialInstitution
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#FinancialInstitution> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#FinancialInstitution> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://schema.org/BankOrCreditUnion> .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#FinancialInstitution> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#Organization> .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#FinancialInstitution> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A bank, investment fund, insurance company or other financial institution whose portfolio exposure to nature-related risks is assessed through biodiversity risk frameworks."@en .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#FinancialInstitution> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Financial Institution"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#FrameworkConcept
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#FrameworkConcept> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#FrameworkConcept> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A concept, disclosure requirement, indicator or metric defined within a disclosure framework. Subclasses represent specific concepts; individuals of this class are not intended."@en .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#FrameworkConcept> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Framework Concept"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#GRIImpactMateriality
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#GRIImpactMateriality> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#GRIImpactMateriality> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#MaterialityBoundary> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#GRIManagementApproach
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#GRIManagementApproach> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#GRIManagementApproach> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#FrameworkConcept> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#GRIOperationsAdjacentProtectedAreas
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#GRIOperationsAdjacentProtectedAreas> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#GRIOperationsAdjacentProtectedAreas> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#ESRSBiodiversitySensitiveArea> .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#GRIOperationsAdjacentProtectedAreas> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#FrameworkConcept> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#GeographicSamplingBias
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#GeographicSamplingBias> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#GeographicSamplingBias> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#DataGap> .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#GeographicSamplingBias> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Systematic under-representation of species occurrences in GBIF/OBIS records for specific geographic regions."@en .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#GeographicSamplingBias> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Geographic Sampling Bias"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#IndustrialClassification
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#IndustrialClassification> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#IndustrialClassification> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A standard system for classifying economic activities into sectors and subsectors (e.g., GICS, CNAE, CIIU, SASB/SICS). Different standards may not be mutually translatable without ambiguity."@en .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#IndustrialClassification> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Industrial Classification Standard"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#InformationLoss
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#InformationLoss> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#InformationLoss> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The loss of material information that occurs when translating a disclosure or target from one framework to another under an incommensurability relationship. Complements bro:hasBridgingCondition by documenting what is lost, not just under what conditions the conversion is admissible."@en .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#InformationLoss> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Information Loss"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#InternalPolicy
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#InternalPolicy> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#InternalPolicy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An organization's internal policy for managing environmental, social, climate or nature-related risks (e.g., an ESCC policy). May partially cover requirements of external disclosure frameworks."@en .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#InternalPolicy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Internal Policy"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#LEAPAssessment
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#LEAPAssessment> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#LEAPAssessment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#Activity> .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#LEAPAssessment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A structured assessment following the TNFD LEAP methodology (Locate, Evaluate, Assess, Prepare), conducted by an organization to identify and assess its nature-related dependencies, impacts, risks and opportunities. Connects the organization, frameworks applied, sectors evaluated, biomes, data sources and gaps identified."@en .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#LEAPAssessment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "LEAP Assessment"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#MaterialityApproach
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#MaterialityApproach> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#MaterialityApproach> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A methodological approach for determining which nature-related impacts, risks and opportunities are material and must be disclosed. Different frameworks apply different approaches (financial, impact, or double materiality) that are not mutually equivalent."@en .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#MaterialityApproach> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Materiality Approach"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#MaterialityBoundary
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#MaterialityBoundary> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#MaterialityBoundary> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The scope and criteria used by a framework to determine which impacts and financial effects are material and must be disclosed."@en .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#MaterialityBoundary> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Materiality Boundary"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#MaterialityResult
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#MaterialityResult> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#MaterialityResult> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The output of a materiality assessment — a ranked or scored set of sectors, locations or impacts identified as material under a specific framework and approach."@en .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#MaterialityResult> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Materiality Result"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#Metric
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#Metric> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#Metric> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#FrameworkConcept> .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#Metric> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A quantitative or semi-quantitative indicator expressed in specific units or using a defined measurement approach."@en .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#Metric> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Metric"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#Organization
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#Organization> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#Organization> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#Organization> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An organization that applies one or more biodiversity risk disclosure frameworks to assess its nature-related dependencies, impacts, risks and opportunities."@en .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#Organization> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Organization"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#PhysicalRisk
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#PhysicalRisk> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#PhysicalRisk> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A nature-related physical risk arising from the degradation of ecosystems or natural capital, including water stress, ecosystem collapse, loss of pollination, erosion or flooding. Corresponds to TNFD and ESRS physical risk category."@en .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#PhysicalRisk> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Physical Risk"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#Portfolio
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#Portfolio> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#Portfolio> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A credit or investment portfolio of a financial institution, composed of assets across multiple economic sectors and geographic locations."@en .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#Portfolio> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Portfolio"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#PriorityLocation
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#PriorityLocation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#PriorityLocation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#FrameworkConcept> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#QualitativeMaterialityScale
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#QualitativeMaterialityScale> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#QualitativeMaterialityScale> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#MaterialityApproach> .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#QualitativeMaterialityScale> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A narrative or categorical approach to assessing materiality of nature-related impacts, without a fixed numerical scale (e.g., GRI 101 impact materiality approach)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#QualitativeMaterialityScale> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Qualitative Materiality Scale"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#QuantitativeMaterialityScale
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#QuantitativeMaterialityScale> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#QuantitativeMaterialityScale> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#MaterialityApproach> .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#QuantitativeMaterialityScale> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A numerical scale used to score materiality of nature-related impacts and dependencies (e.g., ENCORE scale 3-9: very low=3, low=4.5, medium=6, high=7.5, very high=9)."@en .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#QuantitativeMaterialityScale> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Quantitative Materiality Scale"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#SBTNAR3TTarget
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#SBTNAR3TTarget> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#SBTNAR3TTarget> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#FrameworkConcept> .
