# https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#SBTNMeanSpeciesAbundance
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#SBTNMeanSpeciesAbundance> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#SBTNMeanSpeciesAbundance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#Metric> .
# 
# https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#Sector
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#Sector> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#Sector> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An economic sector associated with potential impacts and dependencies on nature, classifiable under international standards such as GICS or SASB/SICS."@en .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#Sector> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Economic Sector"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#SectorPriority
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#SectorPriority> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#SectorPriority> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A context-dependent ordered entry assigning an economic sector an ordinal position within a materiality result."@en .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#SectorPriority> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Sector Priority"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#SemanticAmbiguity
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#SemanticAmbiguity> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#SemanticAmbiguity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A documented case of semantic ambiguity in the correspondence between two industrial classification standards, where a category in one standard maps to multiple non-equivalent categories in another, or vice versa."@en .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#SemanticAmbiguity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Semantic Ambiguity"@en .
# 
