<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#CIIUtoGICSInformationLoss> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A CIIU-to-GICS conversion loses national classification detail and cannot preserve a bijective sector correspondence; multiple CIIU activities may collapse into one GICS sector and some activities require expert interpretation."@en .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#CIIUtoGICSInformationLoss> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "CIIU to GICS Information Loss"@en .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#CIIUtoGICSInformationLoss> <https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#hasBridgingCondition> "Manually align each CIIU code with the most representative GICS or SASB/SICS sector and document all ambiguous, multi-to-one and one-to-many correspondences."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#CNAE
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#CNAE> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#CNAE> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#IndustrialClassification> .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#CNAE> <https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#hasAmbiguity> <https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#CNAEtoGICSAmbiguity> .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#CNAE> <https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#hasInformationLoss> <https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#CNAEtoGICSInformationLoss> .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#CNAE> <https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#incommensurableWith> <https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#GICS> .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#CNAE> <https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#mappableTo> <https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#GICS> .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#CNAE> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Brazilian national industrial classification used by financial institutions for portfolio reporting. Requires manual mapping to GICS for TNFD/ENCORE assessments."@en .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#CNAE> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "CNAE"@en .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#CNAE> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "CNAE (Brazilian national classification) and GICS (international standard used by ENCORE/TNFD) do not maintain a bijective correspondence. Multiple CNAE codes may map to one GICS sector and vice versa, generating semantic ambiguity in sector-level materiality assessments."@en .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#CNAE> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Classificação Nacional de Atividades Econômicas"@en .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#CNAE> <https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#hasBridgingCondition> "A lossy correspondence is admissible when each CNAE code is manually mapped to the most representative GICS sector, with explicit documentation of multi-to-one and one-to-many correspondences. This mapping was performed by EY during the CEBDS Brazil LEAP pilot and required significant expert effort. The result is not automatically reversible."@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#CNAEtoGICSAmbiguity
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#CNAEtoGICSAmbiguity> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#CNAEtoGICSAmbiguity> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#SemanticAmbiguity> .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#CNAEtoGICSAmbiguity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Documented semantic ambiguity in the CNAE-to-GICS mapping required for TNFD/ENCORE assessments. Brazilian CNAE categories do not maintain a bijective correspondence with GICS sectors — multiple CNAE codes may map to one GICS sector or vice versa. Required significant manual effort in the CEBDS Brazil pilot."@en .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#CNAEtoGICSAmbiguity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "CNAE to GICS Semantic Ambiguity"@en .
# 
# https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#CNAEtoGICSInformationLoss
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#CNAEtoGICSInformationLoss> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual> .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#CNAEtoGICSInformationLoss> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#InformationLoss> .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#CNAEtoGICSInformationLoss> <https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#sourceConcept> <https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#CNAE> .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#CNAEtoGICSInformationLoss> <https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#targetConcept> <https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#GICS> .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#CNAEtoGICSInformationLoss> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A CNAE-to-GICS conversion loses Brazilian activity-code specificity and is not automatically reversible because the standards contain multi-to-one and one-to-many sector correspondences."@en .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#CNAEtoGICSInformationLoss> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "CNAE to GICS Information Loss"@en .
<https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#CNAEtoGICSInformationLoss> <https://w3id.org/biodivrisK-onto#hasBridgingCondition> "Manually map every CNAE code to the most representative GICS sector and explicitly record ambiguous and non-bijective correspondences."@en .
# 
